   269	## 3. Exact finite computation specification
   270	
   271	### 3.1 Degree boxes and graph model
   272	
   273	A box is
   274	
   275	```text
   276	B=(e; ds, dp, dc1, dq, dr, dg).
   277	```
   278	
   279	Here `eta=sum(et_j Z^j,0<=j<=e)` has **exact** degree `e`, while the other six
   280	entries are honest upper bounds for `s,p,C1,q,r,G`; zero is included. The
   281	sentinel `-infinity` forces the corresponding polynomial to zero. Optional
   282	exact-degree subcharts saturate that polynomial's named leader; no cap is ever
   283	reported as an exact degree. This removes the old `sig`/vanished-leader bug
   284	(`review:305-314`). A corrected first wave may use
   285	`e=0..2`, `ds=0..4`, and `dp=dc1=dq=dr=dg=N` for `N=3..6`; those 60 boxes are
   286	a schedule, not a completeness bound.
   287	
   288	Use safe ASCII coefficient names. The seven mathematical unknowns remain those
   289	of Section 1, but introduce coefficient-vector auxiliaries `cc2,ee1,dd1` to
   290	avoid division. Safe `Z`-degree caps are
   291	
   292	```text
   293	dC2 = 1+e+max(ds,e),
   294	dE1 = max(2e,dg),
   295	dD1 = max(3e,e+dg).
   296	```
   297	
   298	Cancellation may lower these degrees, so their leaders are not saturated.
   299	Define `ee2=bb*Z*eta^2`, `dd2=aa*Z*eta^3`, and impose every `Z`-coefficient of
   300	
   301	```text
   302	gc2 = 2bb*cc2-Z*eta*(3aa*s+c5*eta),
   303	ge1 = ee1-dZ(ee2)-gg,
   304	gd1 = 2bb*(dd1-dZ(dd2))-3aa*eta*gg.                 (Graph)
   305	```
   306	
   307	On `bb!=0` this graph is exactly the corrected seven-polynomial model, not a
   308	relaxation (`review:258-265,316-322`).
