+## 1. Conventions and the corrected seven-equation system
+
+Work over the complex numbers `C` (hence characteristic zero). Put
+
+```text
+RR = C[A,U,Z]/(U^2-A-A^2 Z),   H=A+A^2 Z,   chi=2+4AZ.
+```
+
+All displayed products commute. The scalars below have zero `Z`-derivative. A prime in this section means only
+`delta=d/dZ`; it is never a label or `d/dV`. Set `deg(0)=-infinity` and, when
+the `(T,V)` valuation is used, `v(0)=+infinity` (`review:45-52,65-67`). There
+are no coefficient levels above two.
+
+Choose constants `a,b,c5,kappa in C` and seven free polynomials
+
+```text
+eta,s,p,C1,q,r,G in C[Z],       a*b*kappa != 0,       eta != 0.
+```
+
+Here `p=C_0`, `q=D_0`, `r=E_0`; `a,b` are the review's `c_1,c_2`. Define,
+in this order,
+
+```text
+E2 = b Z eta^2,                         D2 = a Z eta^3,
+C2 = Z eta(3a s+c5 eta)/(2b),           E1 = E2' + G,
+D1 = D2' + (3a/(2b)) eta G,
+P  = p + A C1 + A^2 C2,                 Q  = q + A D1 + A^2 D2,
+R0 = r + A E1 + A^2 E2,                 S0 = s.
+```
+
+Division is licensed by `b!=0`; Section 3 gives the denominator-free graph
+encoding. In the named chart `T=A^-1`, `V=U/A`, `Z=V^2-T`, let `v` be the
+`T`-adic valuation and set `alpha=-v(f)`, `beta=-v(g)`. Thus `L_1=L_2=0`, and
+nonzero `D2,E2` put the pair in cell `(alpha,beta)=(3,2)`. The structural parametrization is not a unique gauge:
+`eta` can be rescaled, and the shear `f -> f+lambda g` shifts `c5`; the
+computation retains `c5` rather than silently fixing it (`review:267-271`).
+
+For orientation, with `f=P+UQ`, `g=R0+US0`, define
+
+```text
+J(X,Y)=X_A Y_Z-X_Z Y_A,
+WA(X,Y)=X_A Y-X Y_A,       WZ(X,Y)=X_Z Y-X Y_Z,
+Even = 2A^2(P_A S0-Q (R0)_A)+4H(J(P,S0)+J(Q,R0))
+       +chi(Q (R0)_Z-P_Z S0),
+Odd  = 2A^2 WA(Q,S0)+4J(P,R0)+4H J(Q,S0)-chi WZ(Q,S0).
+```
+
+These are the reviewed even/odd parts of `{f,g}` (`r2:43-59`). Equality below
+means a polynomial identity in `C[Z]`, coefficient by coefficient, not equality
+at sampled values. The corrected residual system is exactly:
+
+```text
+O0: 4(C1 r'-p' E1)+2(q s'-q' s)=0.
+
+O1: 8(C2 r'-p' E2)+4(C1 E1'-C1' E1)
+    +6D1 s'-2D1' s+4Z(q s'-q' s)=0.
+
+O2: 4(C1 E2'-2C1' E2+2C2 E1'-C2' E1)
+    +10D2 s'-2D2' s+2D1 s+8Z D1 s'-4Z D1' s=0.
+
+E0: 2(q r'-p' s)=kappa.
+
+E1: 6D1 r'-4q' E1+2q E1'+4C1 s'-2C1' s
+    +4Z(q r'-p' s)=0.
+
+E2: 10D2 r'-8q' E2+2q E2'+6D1 E1'-4D1' E1
+    +2C1 s+8C2 s'-2C2' s+8Z D1 r'
+    +4Z(q E1'-q' E1+C1 s'-C1' s)=0.
+
+E3: 4C2 s-4q E2-2D1 E1+6D1 E2'-8D1' E2
+    +10D2 E1'-4D2' E1
+    +Z(8C2 s'-4C2' s-8q' E2+4q E2'
+       +8D1 E1'-4D1' E1+12D2 r')=0.
+```
+
+They are `[A^0..2]Odd=0`, `[A^0]Even=kappa`, and
+`[A^1..3]Even=0`. The parametrization has already consumed `[A^3]Odd`;
+the corrected identity below consumes `[A^4]Even`; `[A^5]Even` then vanishes,
+and no higher coefficient occurs. This is the review-corrected `7/7` model
+(`review:204-265`), not the rejected r2 system.
+
+## 2. Desk consequences and a serious termination attempt
+
+### 2.1 The correction really eliminates `D1`
+
+Direct collection, with every prime equal to `d/dZ`, gives (`review:219-250`)
+
+```text
+[A^4]Even = -2D2 E1-4D1 E2+10D2 E2'-8D2' E2
+ +Z(8D1 E2'+12D2 E1'-8D1' E2-4D2' E1).
+```
+
+Put `F=D1-D2'` and `G=E1-E2'`. After `E2=bZ eta^2` and
+`D2=aZ eta^3`, this is `2Z eta` times
+
+```text
+3a eta(2Z G' eta-G eta-2Z G eta')
+-2b(2Z F' eta-F eta-4Z F eta').
+```
+
+For `K=2bF-3a eta G`, its vanishing is equivalent to
+
+```text
+2Z eta K'-eta K-4Z eta' K=0.
+```
+
+The removed factor `2Z eta` is a nonzero polynomial in the domain `C[Z]`;
+there is no pointwise inversion at a root of `eta`.
+If `K!=0`, `deg K=k` and `deg eta=e`, the coefficient at degree `e+k` is
+`eta_e K_k(2k-1-4e)`. The parenthesis is odd and cannot vanish. Hence `K=0`
+and
+
+```text
+2bF=3a eta G,   D1=D2'+(3a/(2b))eta G.
+```
+
+This is already a termination-by-degree argument, but only for the auxiliary
+`K`; it does not terminate the seven-polynomial system.
+
+### 2.2 Trying the same argument on `O2`
+
+Isolate the `C1` terms in `O2`:
+
+```text
+O2 = L_eta(C1)+R,
+L_eta(Y)=4b[Y(eta^2+2Z eta eta')-2Z eta^2 Y'].
+```
+
+For nonzero `Y` of degree `m`, `L_eta(Y)` has degree `m+2e` and leading
+coefficient `4b eta_e^2 Y_m(2e+1-2m)`, again with a nonzero odd multiplier.
+Thus `L_eta` is injective. To see what degree count actually does, put
+`sigma=deg s`, `g=deg G`, and write the nonzero leading coefficients as
+`X=eta_e`, `S=s_sigma`, `W=G_g`. Expanding the remainder gives four possible
+top families:
+
+| family | degree | leading coefficient |
+|---|---:|---|
+| `s`, no `G` | `3e+sigma` | `6a X^3 S(e+1)(2sigma-1)` |
+| `c5`, no `G` | `4e` | `2c5 X^4(2e+1)(2e-1)` |
+| `sG` | `e+sigma+g` | `(3a/b)XSW(2g+2sigma-4e-1)` |
+| `c5 G` | `2e+g` | `(2c5/b)X^2W(2g-2e-1)` |
+
+A family is omitted when its named factor is zero. Away from the walls
+`sigma=e` and `g=2e`, the unique largest family is nonzero and `O2` merely
+forces
+
+```text
+deg C1 = deg R-2e
+```
+
+and determines its leading coefficient. On a wall, leading families may
+cancel, so the next coefficient must be inspected; treating the nominal degree
+as exact there would be the vanished-leader fallacy. Nothing in this count
+bounds `e` or `sigma`.
+
+Now take the full section `G=0`; the corrected identity also gives `F=0`.
+The shear `f -> f+lambda g` fixes `g,F,G,kappa` and, since `L1=L2=0`, fixes
+`D1,D2`; it sends `c5` to `c5+2lambda b^2`. Hence
+`lambda=-c5/(2b^2)` safely normalizes `c5=0` throughout this section.
+
+Put `d=3a/(2b)`, `e0=Z eta^2`, and write `C1=d h`. Direct substitution factors
+`O2` exactly as
+
+```text
+O2=6a[(h-h0)e0'-2(h-h0)'e0],       h0=(Z eta)'s.
+```
+
+A nonzero homogeneous difference of degree `m` has the nonzero odd leading
+multiplier `2e+1-2m`. Therefore
+
+```text
+C1=(3a/(2b))(Z eta)'s                                      (2.1)
+```
+
+is the unique polynomial solution of `O2`.
+
+The corner `e=0` already terminates. With
+`B=b eta^2`, `A0=a eta^3`, `t=3a eta/(2b)`, equations `E3,E2` reduce to
+
+```text
+4Z^2 I=0,       6Z I+2Bq=0,       I:=3A0 r'-2B q'+t s s'.
+```
+
+The domain property gives `I=0`; thus `q=0`, `r=r0-s^2/(4B)`, and `E0` makes `p',s` nonzero constants; then
+`E1=2kappa Z`, a contradiction. If instead `s=0` and `e>=1`, (2.1) gives
+`C1=C2=0`; `O0,E0` force `p'=0` and `q,r'` nonzero constants, contradicting
+`T=0` directly: its eta leader has degree `6e`, whereas with `deg q=0` its
+only q leader has degree `3e+1<6e`. It remains only `e>=1`, `s!=0`.
+
+Write `sigma=deg s`, `X=eta_e`, `S=s_sigma`, `m=deg q`, `n=deg r`, and let
+`mathcalE2,mathcalE3` be the left sides of `E2,E3`. In
+
+```text
+T=2Z eta*mathcalE2-(3eta+4Z eta')*mathcalE3
+```
+
+the `r'` terms cancel. The `q`, eta-only, and `s` leaders have respectively
+
+```text
+degree 3e+m+1,       coefficient 4b X^3 q_m(1+4em);
+degree 6e,           coefficient -12ab X^6 e^2(2e-1)(4e+3);
+degree 2e+2sigma+1,  coefficient -(6ae/b)X^2S^2(4sigma-2e-1).
+```
+
+Every displayed factor is nonzero, and the last two degrees have opposite
+parity. Therefore, putting `Dlo=12e^2-4e+1` and
+`Dhi=1+4e(2sigma-e)`, one obtains
+
+```text
+sigma<=2e-1:  m=3e-1,
+ q_m=3aX^3 e^2(2e-1)(4e+3)/Dlo;
+
+sigma>=2e:    m=2sigma-e,
+ q_m=3aeS^2(4sigma-2e-1)/(2b^2 X Dhi).
+```
+
+The four leaders in `E3` then force
+
+```text
+sigma<=2e-1:  deg r=2e-1,
+ r_n=bX^2 e^2(4e^2+8e-7)/Dlo;
+
+sigma>=2e:    deg r=2sigma-2e,
+ r_n=S^2(8e sigma-(2e+1)^2)/(4bX^2 Dhi).
+```
+
+The denominators and displayed integer numerators are nonzero in their stated
+chambers. Finally eliminate `p'` between `O0` and `E0`, without division:
+
+```text
+2(s C1-E1 q)r'+kappa E1+q s s'-q' s^2=0.                 (2.2)
+```
+
+In the lower chamber, the first term has degree `7e-3`, while the last two have
+degrees at most `7e-4` and `2e`: contradiction. In the upper chamber, put
+`H=sC1-E1q`. Its leading coefficient is
+
+```text
+H_top=(3aXS^2/(2b))*(4e sigma+2e+1)/Dhi.
+```
+
+The degree-`4sigma-e-1` coefficient of (2.2) is
+`(sigma-e)(4r_n H_top-S^2q_m)`. In fact the bracket equals
+
+```text
+-(3aS^4/(2b^2 X Dhi^2))*P,
+```
+
+where
+
+```text
+P=(2e+1)[(2e+1)(2e^2+e+1)-8e^2 sigma].
+```
+
+The inner factor is strictly negative for `sigma>=2e`, `e>=1`. This is the
+second contradiction. Thus the serious degree push proves the whole section
+
+```text
+EMPTY[F=G=0].
+```
+
+This is a new desk derivation from the corrected system, not a claim quoted
+from the charged review. Any live cell has `G!=0` and
+`F=(3a/(2b))eta G!=0`. For that remaining section the four-family `O2` table
+generically determines `deg C1` and has genuine cancellation walls; no global
+termination in `eta,s` follows. Type
+`OPEN[ETA-S-DEGREE-TERMINATION,G!=0]` and proceed to exact finite boxes.
+
+## 3. Exact finite computation specification
+
+### 3.1 Degree boxes and graph model
+
+A live-branch box is
+
+```text
+B=(e,g; ds, dp, dc1, dq, dr).
+```
+
+Here `eta=sum(et_j Z^j,0<=j<=e)` and
+`G=sum(gg_j Z^j,0<=j<=g)` have **exact** degrees `e,g`; Section 2 proves the
+omitted `G=0` section empty. The other five entries are honest upper bounds for
+`s,p,C1,q,r`, with zero included. The sentinel `-infinity` forces the named
+polynomial to zero. Optional exact-degree subcharts saturate that polynomial's
+leader; no cap is ever reported as exact. This removes the old
+`sig`/vanished-leader bug (`review:305-314`). A corrected first wave may use
+`e=0..2`, `g=0..6`, `ds=0..4`, and `dp=dc1=dq=dr=N` for `N=3..6`; those boxes
+are a schedule, not a completeness bound.
+
+Use safe ASCII coefficient names. The seven mathematical unknowns remain those
+of Section 1, but introduce coefficient-vector auxiliaries `cc2,ee1,dd1` to
+avoid division. Safe `Z`-degree caps are
+
+```text
+dC2 = 1+e+max(ds,e),
+dE1 = max(2e,g),
+dD1 = max(3e,e+g).
+```
+
+Cancellation may lower these degrees, so their leaders are not saturated.
+Define `ee2=bb*Z*eta^2`, `dd2=aa*Z*eta^3`, and impose every `Z`-coefficient of
+
+```text
+gc2 = 2bb*cc2-Z*eta*(3aa*s+c5*eta),
+ge1 = ee1-dZ(ee2)-gg,
+gd1 = 2bb*(dd1-dZ(dd2))-3aa*eta*gg.                 (Graph)
+```
+
+On `bb!=0` this graph is exactly the corrected seven-polynomial model, not a
+relaxation (`review:258-265,316-322`).
+
+### 3.2 Rings, named maps, and construction
+
+The engine adapter must print its product and exact version. Declare
+
+```text
+Par_B = QQ[aa,bb,c5,kap,
+           et_0..et_e, ss_0.., pp_0.., cc1_0..,
+           qq_0.., rr_0.., gg_0.., cc2_0.., ee1_0.., dd1_0..], grevlex;
+Build_B = Par_B[AA,ZZ], lex with AA>ZZ.
+```
+
+The displayed order is the complete generator order. The rational equations
+are interpreted over the algebraic closure inside `C`. Declare the maps before
+any application:
+
+```text
+lift_B : Par_B -> Build_B       (listed parameter generator -> same listed image),
+at00_B : Build_B -> Par_B       (parameters fixed, AA->0, ZZ->0).
+```
+
+Assert every generator image and `at00_B(lift_B(x))=x` on all parameter
+generators. Matching printed names are not coercions. Define wrappers
+`dA(h)=partial(h,AA)`, `dZ(h)=partial(h,ZZ)` and assert
+
+```text
+dA(AA)=dZ(ZZ)=1,   dA(ZZ)=dZ(AA)=0.
+```
+
+Only then build the templates from `lift_B` images:
+
+```text
+PP=pp+AA*cc1+AA^2*cc2;          QQp=qq+AA*dd1+AA^2*dd2;
+RR0=rr+AA*ee1+AA^2*ee2;         SS0=ss;
+HH=AA+AA^2*ZZ;                  chi=2+4*AA*ZZ.
+```
+
+Construct `even_br,odd_br` from Section 1 using `dA,dZ`. Explicitly set all
+levels above two to zero; do not rely on an array ending there.
+
+Define `coefA(h,n)` and `coefZ(h,j)` by the requested exponents, never by
+zipping a sparse list. For every extraction assert
+
+```text
+h = sum_n coefA(h,n)*AA^n,
+coefA(h,n) = sum_j coefZ(coefA(h,n),j)*ZZ^j.
+```
+
+After both extractions, assert `AA,ZZ` absent, then apply the already named map
+to land in `Par_B`. Extraction is not evaluation; applying `at00_B` before
+extracting would be wrong.
+
+### 3.3 The ideal and exact decision
+
+Let `Jgraph_B` contain all extracted `Z`-coefficients of `(Graph)`. Before the
+decision ideal, reduce the following in the declared quotient by `Jgraph_B`:
+
+```text
+[AA^3]odd_br,   [AA^4]even_br,   [AA^5]even_br,
+all higher AA coefficients.
+```
+
+All must have exact normal form zero; otherwise abort with `MODEL_BUG`. This
+checks the consumed `C2`, corrected `F/G`, and leading-form identities. Also
+compare the seven lower extracted coefficients term-for-term with Section 1.
+
+Define
+
+```text
+I_B = Jgraph_B
+    + <all ZZ coefficients of all AA coefficients of odd_br>
+    + <all ZZ coefficients of all AA coefficients of even_br-kap>.
+```
+
+Using every actual coefficient is deliberately redundant: after preflight it
+equals the graph plus the seven lower families, while preventing a future
+omission of `[A^4]Even` (`review:278-285`). Put
+
+```text
+Delta_B=aa*bb*kap*et_e*gg_g
+```
+
+times only those additional leaders explicitly declared exact/nonzero in a
+subchart. Compute `Sat_B=I_B:(Delta_B)^infinity`. The `sat()` adapter must
+extract the ideal component, reject warnings/error objects, and assert its
+coefficient field, parent ring, generator order, and monomial order. Declare
+`EMPTY(B)` exactly when the normal form of `1` modulo `Sat_B` is zero—not by
+object or string equality. As an independent saturation control, the unit-ideal
+verdict must agree with the Rabinowitsch ideal
+`rab_lift_B(I_B)+<inv_Delta*rab_lift_B(Delta_B)-1>` in the flat ring
+`Rab_B=QQ[<the same ordered parameter generators>,inv_Delta]`, grevlex with
+`inv_Delta` last. Declare
+`rab_lift_B:Par_B->Rab_B`, list and assert every generator image, and only then
+apply it.
+
+## 4. Controls, evidence semantics, and live-cell flag protocol
+
+The controls run through the identical ring, named-map, extraction, ideal, and
+saturation adapters as a decision box.
+
+**Positive control: a finite jet of an actual formal solution.** The corrected
+Theorem 3.2 supplies unrestricted formal lifts with two independent `C[Z]`
+kernel freedoms at every positive level; it does not supply a terminating
+polynomial or a terminal `(3,2)` point (`review:58-112,129-135`). Use the
+explicit formal branch
+
+```text
+kappa=2,       f=Z,       g=U*sum_(n>=0) L_n A^n,
+L_0=-1,        L_n=-(2n Z/(2n+1))L_(n-1).
+```
+
+Thus `L_n=(-1)^(n+1)(2n)!!/(2n+1)!! Z^n`. For its truncation through `J`, direct
+substitution in the original formulas gives
+
+```text
+Odd=0,
+Even=2-4(J+1)Z L_J A^(J+1), hence Even=2 mod A^(J+1).
+```
+
+At `J=3` the exact test vector is (`review:324-339`)
+
+```text
+f=Z,
+g=U(-1+(2/3)AZ-(8/15)A^2Z^2+(16/35)A^3Z^3),
+Odd=0,       Even=2-(256/35)A^4Z^4.
+```
+
+The finite-jet ideal through `A^3` must be proper and the displayed witness
+must verify directly, including its expected nonzero `A^4` remainder. Do not
+impose the terminal-cell graph on this control.
+
+**Negative control.** Encode the complete `(3,1)` specialization in the same
+pipeline: `R0=r`, `S0=s`, `E1=E2=L1=L2=0`, `D2=cp*Z*s^3`, with all remaining
+degree-capped coefficients retained. Extract every actual `A,Z` coefficient of
+`even_br-kap,odd_br`, through their computed top exponents, and saturate by
+`cp*kap*s_leader` on each exact nonzero-`s` chart. It must return `EMPTY`; a
+proper ideal diagnoses the implementation, not the proved cell elimination
+(`review:178-202,324-327`). The desk-closed full `F=G=0` section, represented
+after its named shear by `G=c5=0`, is an additional negative regression family.
+
+**Meaning of `EMPTY`.** `Sat_B=(1)` proves only that this faithfully encoded
+finite box has no complex point with `Delta_B!=0`. Even if every scheduled box
+is empty, record only `FINITE-BOX-EMPTY-EVIDENCE`; `OPEN[A2-CELL-32]` remains,
+because no promoted theorem bounds the polynomial degrees (`review:341-346`).
+
+**Meaning of `NONEMPTY`.** A proper saturated ideal stops the batch immediately
+and emits
+
+```text
+NONEMPTY_PROVISIONAL
+LIVE[A2-CELL-32,B]
+ROUTE[DEGREE-8-VERIFY]
+```
+
+This opens the live degree-8-cell protocol; it is not yet a certified degree-8
+cell. Extract an exact algebraic witness and, without using the saturated ideal,
+perform all of the following postchecks:
+
+1. `Delta_B` and every chart leader are nonzero.
+2. All graph identities hold, and `P,Q,R0,S0` reconstruct through the declared
+   maps with the claimed caps and no level above two.
+3. The original, unsimplified `even_br-kap` and `odd_br` vanish coefficientwise
+   in `A,Z`; recompute `(alpha,beta)=(3,2)` in the `(T,V)` chart.
+4. Independently verify the unencoded field condition
+   `[K:C(f,g)]=4`. Until it holds, type the result only
+   `LIVE[CONSTANT-BRACKET-CANDIDATE]`; only then promote
+   `LIVE[DEGREE-8]` (`review:347-349`).
+
+Any failed postcheck is a spurious projection/model result and triggers an
+adapter audit. This is the coordinator's mandatory `NONEMPTY` postcheck rule
+(`integration:89-90`), made explicit for CELL-32.
+
+## 5. Nine dialect lessons: implementation and checklist pass
+
+The eight catalogued lessons are extracted from `review:287-346`; the ninth is
+the charged named-map-before-application rule.
+
+1. **Identifier hygiene.** Use unique portable ASCII names; avoid protected
+   `I,E,Q`, function-shaped generators, and collisions with structural `chi`.
+2. **Derivative dialect.** Use tested `dA,dZ` wrappers; no prime token appears
+   in code and argument order is fixed.
+3. **Ring determinism.** State the exact field, complete ordered generators,
+   block/monomial orders, and distinguish parameter and construction rings.
+4. **Coefficient discipline.** Extract explicit exponents, assert
+   reconstruction and landing ring, and never zip a sparse coefficient list.
+5. **Degree discipline.** Derive partial-`Z` caps from the formulas, explicitly
+   zero every forbidden `A` level, and never use total degree as `Z` degree.
+6. **Zero/leader discipline.** Give zero its own branch and degree
+   `-infinity`; a cap is not an exact degree. Normal-form and zero-test before
+   asking for a remainder's degree.
+7. **Graphs, denominators, and saturation.** Declare every auxiliary, impose
+   its defining graph coefficientwise, retain cleared factors in the
+   saturation open set, unwrap `sat()` and test `(1)` by `NF(1)=0`.
+8. **Controls and verdict semantics.** Positive and negative controls use the
+   same adapter; `EMPTY` stays box-local and `NONEMPTY` stays provisional until
+   exact postcheck.
+9. **Named map before application.** Every inclusion, specialization,
+   flattening, reconstruction, or coefficient-ring coercion gets a name,
+   domain, codomain, ordered image list, and image assertions before its first
+   use. Inline `map(...)(expression)` is forbidden. Coefficient extraction
+   precedes the named map; it is not itself evaluation.
+
