+## 3. Exact finite computation specification
+
+### 3.1 Degree boxes and graph model
+
+A live-branch box is
+
+```text
+B=(e,g; ds, dp, dc1, dq, dr).
+```
+
+Here `eta=sum(et_j Z^j,0<=j<=e)` and
+`G=sum(gg_j Z^j,0<=j<=g)` have **exact** degrees `e,g`; Section 2 proves the
+omitted `G=0` section empty. The other five entries are honest upper bounds for
+`s,p,C1,q,r`, with zero included. The sentinel `-infinity` forces the named
+polynomial to zero. Optional exact-degree subcharts saturate that polynomial's
+leader; no cap is ever reported as exact. This removes the old
+`sig`/vanished-leader bug (`review:305-314`). A corrected first wave may use
+`e=0..2`, `g=0..6`, `ds=0..4`, and `dp=dc1=dq=dr=N` for `N=3..6`; those boxes
+are a schedule, not a completeness bound.
+
+Use safe ASCII coefficient names. The seven mathematical unknowns remain those
+of Section 1, but introduce coefficient-vector auxiliaries `cc2,ee1,dd1` to
+avoid division. Safe `Z`-degree caps are
+
+```text
+dC2 = 1+e+max(ds,e),
+dE1 = max(2e,g),
+dD1 = max(3e,e+g).
+```
+
+Cancellation may lower these degrees, so their leaders are not saturated.
+Define `ee2=bb*Z*eta^2`, `dd2=aa*Z*eta^3`, and impose every `Z`-coefficient of
+
+```text
+gc2 = 2bb*cc2-Z*eta*(3aa*s+c5*eta),
+ge1 = ee1-dZ(ee2)-gg,
+gd1 = 2bb*(dd1-dZ(dd2))-3aa*eta*gg.                 (Graph)
+```
+
+This is a mathematical graph display; code constructs it only after the
+`dZ` wrapper and ring maps are declared and tested in Section 3.2.
+On `bb!=0` this graph is exactly the corrected seven-polynomial model, not a
+relaxation (`review:258-265,316-322`).
+
+### 3.2 Rings, named maps, and construction
+
+The engine adapter must print its product and exact version. Declare
+
+```text
+gens_B = (aa,bb,c5,kap;
+          (et_j)_(0<=j<=e), (ss_j)_(0<=j<=ds),
+          (pp_j)_(0<=j<=dp), (cc1_j)_(0<=j<=dc1),
+          (qq_j)_(0<=j<=dq), (rr_j)_(0<=j<=dr),
+          (gg_j)_(0<=j<=g), (cc2_j)_(0<=j<=dC2),
+          (ee1_j)_(0<=j<=dE1), (dd1_j)_(0<=j<=dD1));
+Par_B = QQ[gens_B], grevlex in exactly that group/index order;
+Build_B = Par_B[AA,ZZ], lex with AA>ZZ.
+```
+
+An upper bound `-infinity` contributes an empty generator group and reconstructs
+the zero polynomial. Thus the displayed parameterized ranges are the complete
+generator order. The rational equations
+are interpreted over the algebraic closure inside `C`. Declare the maps before
+any application:
+
+```text
+lift_B : Par_B -> Build_B       (listed parameter generator -> same listed image),
+coeff_flat_B : Build_B -> Par_B (parameters fixed, AA->0, ZZ->0).
+```
+
+Assert every generator image and `coeff_flat_B(lift_B(x))=x` on all parameter
+generators. Matching printed names are not coercions. Define wrappers
+`dA(h)=partial(h,AA)`, `dZ(h)=partial(h,ZZ)` and assert
+
+```text
+dA(AA)=dZ(ZZ)=1,   dA(ZZ)=dZ(AA)=0.
+```
+
+Only then reconstruct every polynomial, derived term, and graph expression in
+`Build_B` (all sums use the exact ranges in `gens_B`):
+
+```text
+etaB=sum_j lift_B(et_j)ZZ^j;     ggB=sum_j lift_B(gg_j)ZZ^j;
+ssB=sum_j lift_B(ss_j)ZZ^j;      ppB=sum_j lift_B(pp_j)ZZ^j;
+cc1B=sum_j lift_B(cc1_j)ZZ^j;    qqB=sum_j lift_B(qq_j)ZZ^j;
+rrB=sum_j lift_B(rr_j)ZZ^j;      cc2B=sum_j lift_B(cc2_j)ZZ^j;
+ee1B=sum_j lift_B(ee1_j)ZZ^j;    dd1B=sum_j lift_B(dd1_j)ZZ^j;
+ee2B=lift_B(bb)*ZZ*etaB^2;       dd2B=lift_B(aa)*ZZ*etaB^3;
+gc2B=2*lift_B(bb)*cc2B-ZZ*etaB*(3*lift_B(aa)*ssB+lift_B(c5)*etaB);
+ge1B=ee1B-dZ(ee2B)-ggB;
+gd1B=2*lift_B(bb)*(dd1B-dZ(dd2B))-3*lift_B(aa)*etaB*ggB;
+PP=ppB+AA*cc1B+AA^2*cc2B;       QQp=qqB+AA*dd1B+AA^2*dd2B;
+RR0=rrB+AA*ee1B+AA^2*ee2B;      SS0=ssB;
+HH=AA+AA^2*ZZ;                   chiB=2+4*AA*ZZ.
+```
+
+Construct `even_br,odd_br` from Section 1 using `dA,dZ,HH,chiB`. Explicitly set all
+levels above two to zero; do not rely on an array ending there.
+
+Define `coefA(h,n)` and `coefZ(h,j)` by the requested exponents, never by
+zipping a sparse list. For every extraction assert
+
+```text
+h = sum_n coefA(h,n)*AA^n,
+coefA(h,n) = sum_j coefZ(coefA(h,n),j)*ZZ^j.
+```
+
+After both extractions, assert `AA,ZZ` absent, then apply exactly
+`coeff_flat_B` and assert that the parent is literally `Par_B`. Define this
+ordered operation as `land_B(h,n,j)`. Extraction is not evaluation; applying
+`coeff_flat_B` before both extractions would be wrong.
