+
+The output below is therefore a corrected exact finite-decision specification,
+not a claimed proof of emptiness. It makes no boundary, flag, cover-series,
+attainment, or exit-price assertion.
+
+## 1. Conventions and the corrected seven-equation system
+
+Work over the complex numbers `C` (hence characteristic zero). Put
+
+```text
+RR = C[A,U,Z]/(U^2-A-A^2 Z),   H=A+A^2 Z,   chi=2+4AZ.
+```
+
+All displayed products commute. The scalars below have zero `Z`-derivative. A prime in this section means only
+`delta=d/dZ`; it is never a label or `d/dV`. Set `deg(0)=-infinity` and, when
+the `(T,V)` valuation is used, `v(0)=+infinity` (`review:45-52,65-67`). There
+are no coefficient levels above two.
+
+Choose constants `a,b,c5,kappa in C` and seven free polynomials
+
+```text
+eta,s,p,C1,q,r,G in C[Z],       a*b*kappa != 0,       eta != 0.
+```
+
+Here `p=C_0`, `q=D_0`, `r=E_0`; `a,b` are the review's `c_1,c_2`. Define,
+in this order,
+
+```text
+E2 = b Z eta^2,                         D2 = a Z eta^3,
+C2 = Z eta(3a s+c5 eta)/(2b),           E1 = E2' + G,
+D1 = D2' + (3a/(2b)) eta G,
+P  = p + A C1 + A^2 C2,                 Q  = q + A D1 + A^2 D2,
+R0 = r + A E1 + A^2 E2,                 S0 = s.
+```
+
+Division is licensed by `b!=0`; Section 3 gives the denominator-free graph
+encoding. In the named chart `T=A^-1`, `V=U/A`, `Z=V^2-T`, let `v` be the
+`T`-adic valuation and set `alpha=-v(f)`, `beta=-v(g)`. Thus `L_1=L_2=0`, and
+nonzero `D2,E2` put the pair in cell `(alpha,beta)=(3,2)`. The structural parametrization is not a unique gauge:
+`eta` can be rescaled, and the shear `f -> f+lambda g` shifts `c5`; the
+computation retains `c5` rather than silently fixing it (`review:267-271`).
+
+For orientation, with `f=P+UQ`, `g=R0+US0`, define
+
+```text
+J(X,Y)=X_A Y_Z-X_Z Y_A,
+WA(X,Y)=X_A Y-X Y_A,       WZ(X,Y)=X_Z Y-X Y_Z,
+Even = 2A^2(P_A S0-Q (R0)_A)+4H(J(P,S0)+J(Q,R0))
+       +chi(Q (R0)_Z-P_Z S0),
+Odd  = 2A^2 WA(Q,S0)+4J(P,R0)+4H J(Q,S0)-chi WZ(Q,S0).
+```
+
+These are the reviewed even/odd parts of `{f,g}` (`r2:43-59`). Equality below
+means a polynomial identity in `C[Z]`, coefficient by coefficient, not equality
+at sampled values. The corrected residual system is exactly:
+
+```text
+O0: 4(C1 r'-p' E1)+2(q s'-q' s)=0.
+
+O1: 8(C2 r'-p' E2)+4(C1 E1'-C1' E1)
+    +6D1 s'-2D1' s+4Z(q s'-q' s)=0.
+
+O2: 4(C1 E2'-2C1' E2+2C2 E1'-C2' E1)
+    +10D2 s'-2D2' s+2D1 s+8Z D1 s'-4Z D1' s=0.
+
+E0: 2(q r'-p' s)=kappa.
+
+E1: 6D1 r'-4q' E1+2q E1'+4C1 s'-2C1' s
+    +4Z(q r'-p' s)=0.
+
+E2: 10D2 r'-8q' E2+2q E2'+6D1 E1'-4D1' E1
+    +2C1 s+8C2 s'-2C2' s+8Z D1 r'
+    +4Z(q E1'-q' E1+C1 s'-C1' s)=0.
+
+E3: 4C2 s-4q E2-2D1 E1+6D1 E2'-8D1' E2
+    +10D2 E1'-4D2' E1
+    +Z(8C2 s'-4C2' s-8q' E2+4q E2'
+       +8D1 E1'-4D1' E1+12D2 r')=0.
+```
+
+They are `[A^0..2]Odd=0`, `[A^0]Even=kappa`, and
+`[A^1..3]Even=0`. The parametrization has already consumed `[A^3]Odd`;
+the corrected identity below consumes `[A^4]Even`; `[A^5]Even` then vanishes,
+and no higher coefficient occurs. This is the review-corrected `7/7` model
+(`review:204-265`), not the rejected r2 system.
+
+## 2. Desk consequences and a serious termination attempt
+
+### 2.1 The correction really eliminates `D1`
+
+Direct collection, with every prime equal to `d/dZ`, gives (`review:219-250`)
+
+```text
+[A^4]Even = -2D2 E1-4D1 E2+10D2 E2'-8D2' E2
+ +Z(8D1 E2'+12D2 E1'-8D1' E2-4D2' E1).
+```
+
+Put `F=D1-D2'` and `G=E1-E2'`. After `E2=bZ eta^2` and
+`D2=aZ eta^3`, this is `2Z eta` times
+
+```text
+3a eta(2Z G' eta-G eta-2Z G eta')
+-2b(2Z F' eta-F eta-4Z F eta').
+```
+
+For `Kaux=2bF-3a eta G`, its vanishing is equivalent to
+
+```text
+2Z eta Kaux'-eta Kaux-4Z eta' Kaux=0.
+```
+
+The removed factor `2Z eta` is a nonzero polynomial in the domain `C[Z]`;
+there is no pointwise inversion at a root of `eta`.
+If `Kaux!=0`, `deg Kaux=k` and `deg eta=e`, the coefficient at degree `e+k` is
+`eta_e (Kaux)_k(2k-1-4e)`. The parenthesis is odd and cannot vanish. Hence `Kaux=0`
+and
+
+```text
+2bF=3a eta G,   D1=D2'+(3a/(2b))eta G.
+```
+
+This is already a termination-by-degree argument, but only for the auxiliary
+`K`; it does not terminate the seven-polynomial system.
+
+### 2.2 Trying the same argument on `O2`
+
+Isolate the `C1` terms in `O2`:
+
+```text
+O2 = L_eta(C1)+R,
+L_eta(Y)=4b[Y(eta^2+2Z eta eta')-2Z eta^2 Y'].
+```
+
+For nonzero `Y` of degree `m`, `L_eta(Y)` has degree `m+2e` and leading
+coefficient `4b eta_e^2 Y_m(2e+1-2m)`, again with a nonzero odd multiplier.
+Thus `L_eta` is injective. To see what degree count actually does, put
+`sigma=deg s`, `g=deg G`, and write the nonzero leading coefficients as
+`X=eta_e`, `S=s_sigma`, `W=G_g`. Expanding the remainder gives four possible
+top families:
+
+| family | degree | leading coefficient |
+|---|---:|---|
+| `s`, no `G` | `3e+sigma` | `6a X^3 S(e+1)(2sigma-1)` |
+| `c5`, no `G` | `4e` | `2c5 X^4(2e+1)(2e-1)` |
+| `sG` | `e+sigma+g` | `(3a/b)XSW(2g+2sigma-4e-1)` |
+| `c5 G` | `2e+g` | `(2c5/b)X^2W(2g-2e-1)` |
+
+A family is omitted when its named factor is zero. Away from the walls
+`sigma=e` and `g=2e`, the unique largest family is nonzero and `O2` merely
+forces
+
+```text
+deg C1 = deg R-2e
+```
+
+and determines its leading coefficient. On a wall, leading families may
+cancel, so the next coefficient must be inspected; treating the nominal degree
+as exact there would be the vanished-leader fallacy. Nothing in this count
+bounds `e` or `sigma`.
+
+Now take the full section `G=0`; the corrected identity also gives `F=0`.
+The shear `f -> f+lambda g` fixes `g,F,G,kappa` and, since `L1=L2=0`, fixes
+`D1,D2`; it sends `c5` to `c5+2lambda b^2`. Hence
+`lambda=-c5/(2b^2)` safely normalizes `c5=0` throughout this section.
+
+Put `d=3a/(2b)`, `e0=Z eta^2`, and write `C1=d h`. Direct substitution factors
+`O2` exactly as
+
+```text
+O2=6a[(h-h0)e0'-2(h-h0)'e0],       h0=(Z eta)'s.
+```
+
+A nonzero homogeneous difference of degree `m` has the nonzero odd leading
+multiplier `2e+1-2m`. Therefore
+
+```text
+C1=(3a/(2b))(Z eta)'s                                      (2.1)
+```
+
+is the unique polynomial solution of `O2`.
+
+The corner `e=0` already terminates. With
+`B=b eta^2`, `A0=a eta^3`, `t=3a eta/(2b)`, equations `E3,E2` reduce to
+
+```text
+4Z^2 I=0,       6Z I+2Bq=0,       I:=3A0 r'-2B q'+t s s'.
+```
+
+The domain property gives `I=0`; thus `q=0`, `r=r0-s^2/(4B)`, and `E0` makes `p',s` nonzero constants; then
+`E1=2kappa Z`, a contradiction. If instead `s=0` and `e>=1`, (2.1) gives
+`C1=C2=0`; `O0,E0` force `p'=0` and `q,r'` nonzero constants, contradicting
+`R23=0` directly: its eta leader has degree `6e`, whereas with `deg q=0` its
+only q leader has degree `3e+1<6e`. It remains only `e>=1`, `s!=0`.
+
+Write `sigma=deg s`, `X=eta_e`, `S=s_sigma`, and let
+`mathcalE2,mathcalE3` be the left sides of `E2,E3`. In
+
+```text
+R23=2Z eta*mathcalE2-(3eta+4Z eta')*mathcalE3
+```
+
+the `r'` terms cancel. The eta-only and `s` leaders always have the first two
+lines below; conditionally, if `q!=0` and `m=deg q`, its leader is the third:
+
+```text
+degree 6e,           coefficient -12ab X^6 e^2(2e-1)(4e+3);
+degree 2e+2sigma+1,  coefficient -(6ae/b)X^2S^2(4sigma-2e-1).
+degree 3e+m+1,       coefficient 4b X^3 q_m(1+4em).
+```
+
+Every displayed factor is nonzero, and the first two degrees have opposite
+parity. If `q=0`, those two unmatched families already contradict `R23=0`.
+Thus `q!=0`; put `m=deg q`. With `Dlo=12e^2-4e+1` and
+`Dhi=1+4e(2sigma-e)`, one obtains
+
+```text
+sigma<=2e-1:  m=3e-1,
+ q_m=3aX^3 e^2(2e-1)(4e+3)/Dlo;
+
+sigma>=2e:    m=2sigma-e,
+ q_m=3aeS^2(4sigma-2e-1)/(2b^2 X Dhi).
